/* book exam traps: Using the pitch circle diameter where the radius belongs: F = T/(nR) = 2T/(nD1). Mixing them halves or doubles the bolt force. | Checking the bolts in shear only. Flange crushing on the bolt, the hub and the flange shear at the hub are all part of the answer. | Checking a bushed pin in shear only. The force acts at the middle of the bush, so the pin also bends, and bending usually governs. | Forgetting the service factor, or using the rated torque for some checks and the design torque for others. | Saying a single universal joint gives a constant output speed. It needs a second joint at the same angle, in phase. */
